        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='3688' id='52' type-v2='text' w='45313' x='12313' y='94375'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='10'>Spielberg (12) and Scorsese (11) lead on volume, but Nolan and Peter Jackson post the highest average rating (8.46).</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='4125' id='53' type-v2='text' w='28125' x='11750' y='62500'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='10'>War (8.18), Biography (8.04) and Drama (8.03) lead; Horror, Action and Thriller trail at 7.89–7.92. A real but narrow ~0.3-point spread.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='4500' id='54' type-v2='text' w='28375' x='70438' y='62313'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='10'>Epic-length films (170+ min) average 8.25 vs 7.94 for 90–130 min. Short films under 90 min (n=39) are the exception at 8.00.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='4438' id='55' type-v2='text' w='28125' x='41063' y='62313'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontsize='10'>More votes go with slightly higher ratings (r ≈ 0.15), but popularity isn’t quality: many top-rated films fly under the radar.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='4125' id='56' type-v2='text' w='57375' x='11938' y='34750'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='10'>No genre leads every decade: the top genre shifts from Drama (1940s) to Crime (1970s), Animation (2000s) and Biography (2020s), among cells with 5+ films.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='10'>Note: Light yellow cells = no films in that genre/decade.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='5438' id='57' type-v2='text' w='28375' x='70500' y='34938'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#ffffff' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='10'>Average rating peaks in the 1930s–1960s (8.14–8.18) and dips to ~7.92 in the 2000s–2010s, even as film count grows over 5×. Older decades have had longer to be filtered by time.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
